<script lang="ts">
 import {MODEL_LABELS} from '@lib/ai/model';
 import {ShieldCheck,Cpu,ArrowUpRight,Search} from 'lucide-svelte';
 let query=$state('');
 const aliases:Record<string,string>={kacamata:'spectacles sunglasses',dompet:'wallet',lampu:'lamp spotlight',parfum:'perfume',ponsel:'cell phone smartphone',buku:'book',kursi:'chair',sepatu:'shoe',tas:'bag'};
 let filtered=$derived.by(()=>{const terms=(aliases[query.trim().toLowerCase()]||query.toLowerCase()).split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean);return MODEL_LABELS.filter(label=>!terms.length||terms.some(term=>label.toLowerCase().includes(term)));});
</script>
<div class="page-title"><div><h1>Model & privacy guide</h1><p>Understand what happens behind every frame.</p></div><a class="btn outline" href="/detect/image">Try detection <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a></div>
<article class="guide">
 <section><Cpu size={25}/><h2>A broader view of everyday objects.</h2><p>Visionary AI uses YOLOE-26s for object regions and instance segmentation, followed by MobileCLIP2-S0 to compare each region with {MODEL_LABELS.length.toLocaleString()} category names. Both models run in your browser, using WebGPU when available and WebAssembly otherwise.</p><p>The vocabulary includes glasses, lamps, wallets, perfume, electronics, furniture, clothing, food, animals, and vehicles. A category being supported does not guarantee recognition in every image. Blurred, small, obscured, unusual, or unfamiliar objects can still be missed or mislabeled.</p><p>The displayed confidence and threshold refer to the YOLOE region proposal score, before label matching. They do not measure certainty in the final object name. Label match is a separate cosine similarity score, not a probability. A question mark means other labels had a similar match. Check uncertain predictions instead of treating their names as verified facts.</p><p>Each scan verifies up to 20 proposed objects. Live counts describe the latest analyzed frame, not unique objects across time. No tracking or identification is used.</p><p>The first analysis downloads about 90 MB of model weights plus label embeddings, then caches verified files when browser storage is available. Matching more categories takes additional computation. Performance varies by device.</p></section>
 <section><ShieldCheck size={25}/><h2>Your data, frame by frame.</h2><p>Camera frames and uploaded photos stay on your device during analysis. Model assets are bundled with the app; runtime binaries load from jsDelivr. No paid AI API or server-side inference is used.</p><p>Only Save sends a compressed snapshot to private Cloudinary storage and its predictions to your account in Neon PostgreSQL. Owner-authorized requests obtain temporary image links. Deleting history removes the account record and queues storage deletion for retry if needed.</p><p>Passwords use Argon2id. Sessions use HttpOnly cookies, short-lived JWTs, rotating refresh sessions, revocation, and CSRF protection. Client-generated predictions remain unverified server-side.</p></section>
 <section><h2>Find a supported category.</h2><label for="category-search">Search English categories, or try kacamata, dompet, lampu, parfum.<input id="category-search" type="search" bind:value={query} placeholder="Search categories…"/></label><p>{filtered.length.toLocaleString()} matching categories</p><div class="labels-list">{#each filtered as label}<span>{label}</span>{:else}<p>No matching category. A supported class list does not cover every possible object.</p>{/each}</div></section>
 <section><h2>Model provenance & licenses</h2><p>YOLOE weights and Ultralytics use AGPL-3.0, with enterprise licensing available. MobileCLIP source and weights use Apple's respective source and model licenses. Model exports, integrity hashes, vocabulary, preprocessing, and validation are documented in the repository's ml directory.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yoloe/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">YOLOE documentation <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/apple-aiml-research/ml-mobileclip" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apple MobileCLIP and licenses <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a></section>
</article>
